chip ymf278b
clock 33868800
samples 40000
mem pcm wavetable.bin
# The envelope, on wave 2 under registers written after the header load:
# a slow attack, decay to a sustain level and a sustain rate, release at
# several rates, attack rate 0 (never sounds), an attack corrected to rate
# 62 (only 63 starts at full level), the sustain level 15 (which
# means 31), rate correction from 0 to 14 at several octaves (with the
# F-number's top bit) against 15 (none), a key on and off in the same
# write burst (ymfm keeps the key on), a second key on while on (no
# restart), a key on during the release (attack from where it is), and
# pseudo-reverb, which from -18dB, in any state but the attack, holds the
# envelope to a fixed slow rate: on channel 10 (on DO1) for the whole log,
# and on channels 5 and 6 in their releases.
0 w 2 05 3 03  # NEW and NEW2: OPL4 mode
0 w 4 2a 5 00 4 42 5 02 4 5a 5 01 4 12 5 02 4 72 5 00 4 a2 5 fa 4 ba 5 4a 4 d2 5 f4 4 42 5 0a 4 72 5 90  # ch 10 on DO1: pseudo-reverb under the key
0 w 4 20 5 00 4 38 5 02 4 50 5 01 4 08 5 02 4 68 5 00 4 98 5 97 4 b0 5 64 4 c8 5 f9 4 68 5 80  # ch 0: AR 9, DR 7, SL 6, SR 4, RR 9
3500 w 4 68 5 00
6000 w 4 21 5 00 4 39 5 02 4 51 5 01 4 09 5 02 4 69 5 00 4 99 5 ca 4 b1 5 f0 4 c9 5 fb 4 69 5 80  # ch 1: SL 15
8000 w 4 69 5 00
9000 w 4 22 5 00 4 3a 5 02 4 52 5 01 4 0a 5 02 4 6a 5 00 4 9a 5 00 4 b2 5 00 4 ca 5 fc 4 6a 5 80  # ch 2: AR 0
9000 w 4 27 5 00 4 3f 5 02 4 57 5 01 4 0f 5 02 4 6f 5 00 4 9f 5 e0 4 b7 5 00 4 cf 5 3c 4 6f 5 80  # ch 7: AR 14 corrected to 62: a gradual attack
9800 w 4 6f 5 00
10000 w 4 6a 5 00
10500 w 4 23 5 00 4 3b 5 02 4 53 5 01 4 0b 5 02 4 6b 5 00 4 9b 5 76 4 b3 5 43 4 cb 5 06 4 6b 5 80  # ch 3: rate correction 0, octave 0
12300 w 4 6b 5 00
13500 w 4 23 5 00 4 3b 5 26 4 53 5 01 4 0b 5 02 4 6b 5 00 4 9b 5 76 4 b3 5 43 4 cb 5 36 4 6b 5 80  # ch 3: rate correction 3, octave 2
15300 w 4 6b 5 00
16500 w 4 23 5 00 4 3b 5 d0 4 53 5 01 4 0b 5 02 4 6b 5 00 4 9b 5 76 4 b3 5 43 4 cb 5 76 4 6b 5 80  # ch 3: rate correction 7, octave -3
18300 w 4 6b 5 00
19500 w 4 23 5 fe 4 3b 5 57 4 53 5 01 4 0b 5 02 4 6b 5 00 4 9b 5 76 4 b3 5 43 4 cb 5 e6 4 6b 5 80  # ch 3: rate correction 14, octave 5
21300 w 4 6b 5 00
22500 w 4 23 5 00 4 3b 5 84 4 53 5 01 4 0b 5 02 4 6b 5 00 4 9b 5 76 4 b3 5 43 4 cb 5 06 4 6b 5 80  # ch 3: rate correction 0, octave -8
24300 w 4 6b 5 00
25500 w 4 23 5 fe 4 3b 5 57 4 53 5 01 4 0b 5 02 4 6b 5 00 4 9b 5 76 4 b3 5 43 4 cb 5 f6 4 6b 5 80  # ch 3: rate correction 15, octave 5
27300 w 4 6b 5 00
28500 w 4 24 5 00 4 3c 5 02 4 54 5 01 4 0c 5 02 4 6c 5 00 4 9c 5 f4 4 b4 5 32 4 cc 5 f8 4 6c 5 80 4 6c 5 00  # ch 4: key on and off at once
29000 w 4 42 5 02  # channel 10 loses its reverb bit, but not its reverb state
29700 w 4 6c 5 80  # a second key on
30000 w 4 72 5 10  # channel 10 keyed off: it stays in reverb
30500 w 4 6c 5 00
30900 w 4 6c 5 80  # key on during the release
32100 w 4 6c 5 00
33000 w 4 25 5 00 4 3d 5 02 4 55 5 01 4 0d 5 02 4 6d 5 00 4 9d 5 f5 4 b5 5 23 4 cd 5 f7 4 3d 5 0a 4 6d 5 80  # ch 5: pseudo-reverb
34500 w 4 6d 5 00
39000 w 4 26 5 00 4 3e 5 02 4 56 5 01 4 0e 5 02 4 6e 5 00 4 9e 5 f0 4 b6 5 00 4 ce 5 f4 4 3e 5 0a 4 6e 5 80  # ch 6: reverb in release
39500 w 4 6e 5 00
